<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trần Nhân Tông</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1258">1258</a>–<a href="/years/1308">1308</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Tran Nhan Tong</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trần Nhân Tông (1258–1308) was emperor of Đại Việt from 1278 to 1293. With the general Trần Hưng Đạo he defeated the Mongol Yuan invasions of 1285 and 1287–1288. After abdicating he became a monk and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truc-lam-zen">Trúc Lâm</a> school of Vietnamese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zen">Zen Buddhism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tran-nhan-tong.jpg" alt="Trần Nhân Tông" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Emperor_Tr%E1%BA%A7n_Nh%C3%A2n_T%C3%B4ng.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
